From 5ce60391b8192a053d86cd29b212136a2d2d56f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:43:23 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 100/122] AcDs: read the SAB of the R2013+ ACIS entities by
 their handle

The SAB data of the R2013+ REGIONs, 3DSOLIDs, BODYs and SURFACEs is in
the data records of the AcDb:AcDsPrototype_1b section. It was searched
for "ACIS BinaryFile" and given to the entities with has_ds_data in
their order. AutoCAD's R2018 files have "ASM BinaryFile4" instead, so
none of their ACIS data was read (example_2018, sample_AC1032), and the
records are not in the order of the entities (example_2013), so the SAB
could go to the wrong entity. Now take the data records of the data
index with their handles, also from blob pages.
The check of the segment index count used the size of the struct, 16,
not the 12 bytes of an entry after the 48 byte segment header, so the
AcDs of sample_base was rejected.

* src/decode.c (acds_rl, acds_rll, acds_segment, acds_blob)
(acds_asm_data): New.
(read_2004_section_acds): Call acds_asm_data.
* src/acds.spec: Remove the search for the SAB. The num_segidx check
with 12 byte entries after the segment header.
* src/common_entity_data.spec: No acis_sab_hdl anymore.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
